Now, the area of a square is side length squared, right? So that would be 25 cm multiplied by 25 cm. Let me calculate that. 25 times 25 is 625. So the area should be 625 cm². Looking at the options, option D is 625 cm². That must be the correct answer. Wait, but let me double-check my steps to make sure I didn't make any mistakes. Perimeter formula for a square is indeed 4s, so dividing 100 by 4 gives 25. Then area is s², which is 25² = 625. Yep, that seems right. None of the other options match this result, so D is definitely the answer.
